WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:10.593
In tutorial 11.5, you'll add
a second step to your sign-in,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.591
so a stolen password is no
longer enough to get in.

00:00:14.621 --> 00:00:18.507
First, click your name at the bottom of
the sidebar, and choose Your account.

00:00:21.096 --> 00:00:24.996
Scroll down to Two-step
verification. It's off for now.

00:00:25.046 --> 00:00:28.399
You can use an authenticator
app, a passkey, or both.

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:32.173
Now, beside Authenticator
app, click Set up.

00:00:34.918 --> 00:00:39.623
Scan the code with an app on your phone,
like Google Authenticator or 1Password.

00:00:39.673 --> 00:00:42.311
Can't scan it? Copy the key instead.

00:00:43.295 --> 00:00:46.950
Then type the 6-digit code the
app shows, and click Turn on.

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:52.816
Alaventra now gives
you ten recovery codes.

00:00:52.866 --> 00:00:55.924
Each one lets you sign in
once, if you lose your phone.

00:00:56.895 --> 00:01:00.420
Click Copy all or Download,
and keep them somewhere safe.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:03.647
They're shown only this once,
so then click I saved them.

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:08.356
Two-step verification is now
on. If you use up your codes,

00:01:08.406 --> 00:01:10.376
click New codes for a fresh set.

00:01:11.681 --> 00:01:15.691
Next, to sign in with your fingerprint,
your face or a security key,

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:17.031
click Add a passkey.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.565
Give it a name, confirm on your
device, and it's listed here.

00:01:21.615 --> 00:01:23.444
You can remove it at any time.

00:01:25.177 --> 00:01:29.904
Finally, under Where you're signed in,
you'll see every device with an open session.

00:01:31.677 --> 00:01:35.902
Sign out any device you don't
recognise, or click Sign out all others,

00:01:35.952 --> 00:01:37.526
and then change your password.

00:01:38.656 --> 00:01:42.756
Now, whenever you sign in,
Alaventra asks for that second step,

00:01:42.806 --> 00:01:45.294
so your websites and reports stay yours.

00:01:46.302 --> 00:01:51.102
So, open Your account, turn on an
authenticator app, save your recovery codes,

00:01:51.152 --> 00:01:53.701
add a passkey, and check
where you're signed in.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:02:01.164
Your account is protected. Next, require
two-step for everyone, in tutorial 11.6.
